><given-names>EA</given-names></name><name><surname>Denlinger</surname><given-names>JL</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Viscosupplementation: a new concept in the treatment of osteoarthritis</article-title><source>J Rheumatol Suppl</source><year>1993</year><volume>39</volume><fpage>3</fpage><lpage>9</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8410881</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B16"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Forrester</surname><given-names>JV</given-names></name><name><surname>Wilkinson</surname><given-names>PC</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Inhibition of leukocyte locomotion by hyaluronic acid</article-title><source>J Cell Sci</source><year>1981</year><volume>48</volume><fpage>315</fpage><lpage>331</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7276093</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B17"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Presti</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Scott</surname><given-names>JE</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Hyaluronan-mediated protective effect against cell damage caused by enzymatically produced hydroxyl (OH<sup>.</sup>) radicals is dependent on hyaluronan molecular mass</article-title><source>Cell Biochem Funct</source><year>1994</year><volume>12</volume><fpage>281</fpage><lpage>288</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7834818</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1002/cbf.290120409</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B18"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Tobetto</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Nakai</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Akatsuka</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Yasui</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Ando</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Hirano</surname><given-names>S</given-